div.div:
Fātŭus , i. m.,

I.another name
				for the prophesying Faunus; also called Fātŭ-ellus ; while his sister, Fauna, who
				prophesied to females, was also called Fātŭa  and Fātŭella ,
					Lact. 1, 22, 9;
					Arn. 5, 18;
					Macr. S. 1, 12;
					Mart. Cap. 2, § 167;
				Just.
				43, 1; Plin. 27, 12, 83, § 117
			(dub.; Jan. fatuos).
